## Why This Is Asked
Tests practical ability to add non-intrusive QA in production, teaches traffic manipulation without risking user impact, and validates multi-DC deployment awareness.

## Key Concepts
- Traffic shadowing vs canary releases
- Nginx mirror and upstream configuration
- Docker-DC/edge proxy routing across DCs
- TLS edge termination and tenant isolation

## Code Example
```nginx
# Example shadow config snippet
upstream prod_api { server prod-api:8080; }
upstream staging_api { server staging-api:8080; }
server {
  listen 443 ssl;
  location /api/ {
    proxy_pass http://prod_api;
    mirror /mirror_to_staging;
  }
  location = /mirror_to_staging {
    proxy_pass http://staging_api;
  }
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you monitor shadowed traffic to ensure no unseen side effects?
- How would you prevent skew if tenant_id headers can be spoofed?

## Why This Is Asked
Tests ability to design cross-DC data residency controls, real-time policy updates, and secure audit logging in a docker-dca setup.

## Key Concepts
- Data residency and cross-DC egress policies
- WASM-based per-tenant policy engine (Wasmtime)
- Vault-driven tenant configs and SPIFFE SVID rotation
- SIEM-based auditing and reproducible bootstrap

## Code Example
```javascript
// Pseudo policy evaluation sketch
function evaluate(event, tenant) {
  if (event.destDC === 'DC-B' && !tenant.optIn) return 'block';
  redact(event.payload, tenant.schema);
  return 'allow';
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you verify policy correctness across DC failover?
- How would you handle policy module hot-reload and versioning?
